    "scenario": "MPLS TE Basic Dynamic Tunnel",
    "goals": "• OSPF area 0, the interface addressing, one Loopback0 per router and an MPLS core with LDP are already configured. {{router1_name}} reaches {{router4_name}} over two equal-cost two-hop paths, one through {{router2_name}} and one through {{router3_name}}. MPLS traffic engineering is not configured yet.\n• Enable MPLS traffic engineering on {{router1_name}}, {{router2_name}}, {{router3_name}} and {{router4_name}}: globally, on every core interface, and inside OSPF area 0 so the TE topology is flooded. Each router must use its Loopback0 address as the MPLS TE router-id.\n• Reserve {{rsvp_bandwidth}} kbps of RSVP bandwidth on every core interface.\n• On {{router1_name}} build the TE tunnel Tunnel{{tunnel_id}} towards {{router4_name}} Loopback0 ({{router4_loopback0_ip}}). Take the tunnel source address from Loopback0 without giving the tunnel its own address, and let the headend compute the path itself with path-option 10.\n• The tunnel must be signalled successfully and reach the up state, and it must be visible as an established LSP on the transit router it selected.",
